                                                                  The electric power steering is designed to provide
                                                                  power assist while driving to operate the steering
                                                                  wheel with light force.
                                                                  When the steering wheel is operated repeatedly or
                                                                  continuously while parking or driving at a very low
                                                                  speed, the power assist for the steering wheel will be
                                                                  reduced. This is to prevent overheating of the electric
                                                                  power steering and protect it from getting damaged.
                                                                  While the power assist is reduced, steering wheel
                                                                  operation will become heavy. When the temperature of
                                                                  the electric power steering goes down, the power
                                                                  assist level will return to normal. Avoid repeating such
                                                                  steering wheel operations that could cause the electric
                                                                  power steering to overheat.
                                                                  You may hear a fricative sound when the steering
                                                                  wheel is operated quickly. However, this is not a
                                                                  malfunction.
                                                                  If the electric power steering warning light
                                                                  illuminates while the engine is running, it may indicate
                                                                  the electric power steering is not functioning properly
                                                                  and may need servicing. Have the electric power
                                                                  steering checked by a NISSAN dealer. (See “Electric
                                                                  power steering warning light” (P.2-14).)
